    <decisions>
        <description>Universal acknowledgement routing rule — every donor gets a receipt. Email path requires: (1) Contact has not opted out of email, AND (2) Contact has a non-blank Email address. Any single failing condition routes to the Task path so the queue member can send the acknowledgement by mail or another channel. No donor-grouping / CMDT / lifetime-donor filtering here — acknowledgement is universal; those tier considerations live in the FQS_Stewardship_Response flow.</description>
        <name>Route_Email_Or_Task</name>
        <label>Route: Email or Task?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Open_Opportunity</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Task Path</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Email_Path</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Contact.HasOptedOutOfEmail</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Contact.Email</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Route_Email_Template</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Email Path</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Scheduled flow that runs daily and processes GiftTransaction records where Status = Paid, TransactionDate is at least 3 days in the past, and AcknowledgementStatus is blank or To Be Sent. The 3-day window lets digital-platform ingest and refunds/reversals settle before an acknowledgement fires. Fee/Payment category is excluded — donors don&apos;t get receipts for processing fees.

Acknowledgement is the universal &quot;we got your gift, thanks, here is your deduction info&quot; touch — every donor with a valid email address receives one. No donor-grouping / CMDT / lifetime-donor filtering; every eligible gift gets a receipt. Tier-based routing lives in the FQS_Stewardship_Response flow, which is a separate follow-up touch that reinforces mission and deepens the donor relationship.

For each qualifying gift the flow: (1) fetches the donor Account and PersonContact; (2) routes to email or task on a universal rule — email if HasOptedOutOfEmail=FALSE AND Email is present, task otherwise; (3) stamps AcknowledgementStatus and AcknowledgementDate accordingly.

Email path: sends the FQS Gift Acknowledgement template (or the Partial Deduction variant when TaxDeductionAmount &lt; CurrentAmount) via the emailSimple v3 template-aware action to the donor PersonContact; sets AcknowledgementStatus = Sent and AcknowledgementDate = today.

Task path: creates a Task owned by the FQS Gift Acknowledgements queue with WhatId set to the soonest open opportunity (or donor Account fallback); sets AcknowledgementStatus = To Be Sent. Queue member completes the personal outreach and closes the task manually, then sets AcknowledgementStatus = Sent.

External-tool contract: donation-form integrations that send their own acknowledgement MUST write GiftTransaction.AcknowledgementStatus = &apos;Sent&apos; back to the record. This flow&apos;s filter (AcknowledgementStatus IS NULL OR = To Be Sent) then naturally excludes those gifts.

Year-end tax receipting is out of scope for automation; see FQS_Tax_Receipt_Date__c for the manual capture field.

Fault connectors on all action and DML elements route to Send_Fault_Email which notifies $User.Email. See .planning/fqs-gift-followup-redesign.md.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>The date boundary used in the Get_GiftTransactions filter. Only gifts whose TransactionDate is on or before this date are included, preserving the 3-day settling window.</description>
        <name>frmThreeDaysAgo</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>{!$Flow.CurrentDate} - 3</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Task activity date. +7 days from today — a standard SLA for personal acknowledgement outreach on gifts that couldn&apos;t receive an auto-email. Tier-scaled SLAs (Major +3, Mid +7, Entry +14) live in the stewardship flow, not here.</description>
        <name>frmTaskActivityDate</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>{!$Flow.CurrentDate} + 7</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Task Description. Explains why the acknowledgement couldn&apos;t be auto-emailed (opt-out or missing email) and surfaces related open opportunity context if any.</description>
        <name>frmTaskDescription</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Personal acknowledgement needed — automated email could not be sent. Reason: &quot; &amp;
IF({!Get_Contact.HasOptedOutOfEmail}, &quot;Contact opted out of email.&quot;,
   IF(ISBLANK({!Get_Contact.Email}), &quot;No email address on Contact.&quot;, &quot;Unknown.&quot;)) &amp;
&quot; Related open opportunity: &quot; &amp;
IF(ISBLANK({!Get_Open_Opportunity.Name}), &quot;none&quot;, {!Get_Open_Opportunity.Name}) &amp; &quot;.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Task subject. Prepends [OPT-OUT — send by mail] when the donor has opted out of email so the queue member knows immediately to use a non-email channel.</description>
        <name>frmTaskSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!Get_Contact.HasOptedOutOfEmail}, &quot;[OPT-OUT — send by mail] &quot;, &quot;&quot;) &amp;
&quot;Acknowledge gift: &quot; &amp;
{!Get_Donor_Account.Name} &amp; &quot; — $&quot; &amp; TEXT({!Loop_GiftTransactions.CurrentAmount})</expression>
    </formulas>
